XiangShan changes for DRVFuzz (apply in the XiangShan checkout: git apply xiangshan-drvfuzz.patch).

DRVFuzz attributes every register write to the PC of the instruction that made
it, so it needs one difftest commit per instruction, and all commits before the
good trap:
  1. Configs.scala: DRVFuzzMinimalConfig / DRVFuzzDefaultConfig = MinimalConfig /
     DefaultConfig with EnableRobCompression = false (like the existing
     NoRobCompressionConfig). With ROB compression several instructions commit
     as one difftest entry and only the group head is reported.
  2. Rob.scala: DiffTrapEvent gets delay = 3 like DiffInstrCommit. Otherwise the
     trap reaches difftest 3 cycles before the last commits, and the emu exits
     without reporting them.
  3. CSRCustom.scala: srnctl.FUSION_ENABLE resets to 0, so instruction fusion
     is off; a fused pair also commits as one instruction.
Observed on the server with the unpatched core: a DRVFuzz program of ~30
instructions produced 16 commit lines; the 5 instructions from lui to add were
one entry, and nothing after the sd before HIT GOOD TRAP.

Made against XiangShan 182b2277c0e4115e39ae396f7d705bc4e20e0def (kunminghu-v3).

diff --git a/src/main/scala/top/Configs.scala b/src/main/scala/top/Configs.scala
index d1516ec..d189457 100644
--- a/src/main/scala/top/Configs.scala
+++ b/src/main/scala/top/Configs.scala
@@ -586,6 +586,20 @@ class NoRobCompressionConfig(n: Int = 1) extends Config(
   })
 )
 
+// DRVFuzz: one difftest commit per instruction, so that every register write
+// appears in the commit trace (ROB compression reports only the group head).
+class DRVFuzzMinimalConfig(n: Int = 1) extends Config(
+  new MinimalConfig(n).alter((site, here, up) => {
+    case XSTileKey => up(XSTileKey).map(_.copy(EnableRobCompression = false))
+  })
+)
+
+class DRVFuzzDefaultConfig(n: Int = 1) extends Config(
+  new DefaultConfig(n).alter((site, here, up) => {
+    case XSTileKey => up(XSTileKey).map(_.copy(EnableRobCompression = false))
+  })
+)
+
 class CVMConfig(n: Int = 1) extends Config(
   new CVMCompile
     ++ new DefaultConfig(n)
